SSTTAANNDDAARRDDSS
     The ssttrrccppyy() and ssttrrnnccppyy() functions conform to ISO/IEC 9899:1990
     (“ISO C90”).  The ssttppccppyy() and ssttppnnccppyy() functions conform to IEEE Std
     1003.1-2008 (“POSIX.1”).

HHIISSTTOORRYY
     The ssttppccppyy() function first appeared in FreeBSD 4.4, and ssttppnnccppyy() was
     added in FreeBSD 8.0.

SSEECCUURRIITTYY CCOONNSSIIDDEERRAATTIIOONNSS
     All of the functions documented in this manual page are easily misused in
     a manner which enables malicious users to arbitrarily change a running
     program's functionality through a buffer overflow attack.

     It is strongly suggested that the ssttrrllccppyy() function be used in almost
     all cases.

     For some, but not all, fixed-length records, non-terminated strings may
     be both valid and desirable.  In that specific case, the ssttrrnnccppyy() func‐
     tion may be most sensible.

